---
title: Multi-agent desired-state planning architecture
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: Multi-agent desired-state planning architecture
  accDescr: Versioned source packages and enabled agent profiles enter a read-only planning core. Pure target adapters produce desired resources, which are coalesced and preflighted before one transactional executor changes the machine and records ownership.

  subgraph Inputs[Declarative inputs]
    Source[Versioned source snapshot] --> Normalize[Validate and normalize]
    Manifest[Manifest v2] --> Normalize
    Profiles[Enabled agent profiles and scopes]
    Specs[Pinned target dialect metadata]
  end

  Normalize --> Components["Canonical packages and components<br/>Skills and MCP servers"]

  subgraph Planning[Read-only planning core]
    Registry[Pure, versioned target adapters]
    Negotiate{"Capability and scope<br/>supported without loss?"}
    Project[Project to desired resources]
    Coalesce[Coalesce identical shared resources]
    Preflight["Preflight<br/>compatibility · collisions · drift · trust · policy"]
    Report[Explain, skip, or require an explicit override]

    Registry --> Negotiate
    Negotiate -->|Supported| Project
    Negotiate -->|Lossy or unsupported| Report
    Project --> Coalesce --> Preflight
  end

  Components --> Negotiate
  Profiles --> Registry
  Specs --> Registry

  Preflight --> Resources["Desired resource graph<br/>owned paths · structured entries · text blocks<br/>logical bindings to agent consumers"]

  subgraph Execution[Central mutation boundary]
    Journal[Recovery journal and staged writes]
    Apply[Transactional executor]
    Ledger[Versioned ownership ledger]

    Journal --> Apply --> Ledger
  end


  Resources --> Journal
  Ledger -.->|Current ownership and digests| Preflight
  Apply --> Result[Installed, partial, blocked, or rolled back result]
